From 7c03df5831b3adbc95f75c3551ee42024558c11a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 05:42:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] test(gateway): native live fixture dumps stacks via
 refcounted frames, not faulthandler watchdog

test_native_gateway_runtime_live exited -11 on a hub runner. The fixture armed
faulthandler.dump_traceback_later(repeat=True), whose native watchdog walks
interpreter frames without the GIL; a thread retiring a code object mid-walk
segfaults the gateway (reproduced: old fixture -11 in 6/6 churn runs).

Replace it with an Event-driven Python thread that snapshots
sys._current_frames() (refcounted, like gateway/sigusr2_stack_dump.py), stopped
and joined when the gateway exits. Add a subprocess regression that runs the real
fixture under dynamic-code churn, and PYTHONFAULTHANDLER=1 in the live harness
so any future native crash prints a backtrace.
